title: The <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**DSU**</span> Enters Government
subtitle: Our choice doesn't matter after all.
view-if: chancellor == "Staal" and not dsu_in_gov and not dsu_was_gov and unionist_in_gov and unionist_leader == "Hughes" and staal_post_time >= 8
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
tags: event
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/nazi_gov.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

= The <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**DSU**</span> Enters Government

With the favorable Hughes being installed at the head of the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>, the party no longer voice loud reservations over the inclusion of the "reasonable" <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**DSU**</span> into the Staal cabinet, to increase its popular backing, and to tame the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> that can be tamed. 

This goes completely against Staal's promise to us, that he'll never let the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> into cabinet if we were to give him a major concession. e have been conned, big time.

- @dsu_in_gov

@dsu_in_gov
title: Crowde enters the cabinet.
on-arrival: {!
Q.dsu_in_gov = 1;
Q.staal_post = 1;
Q.vice_chancellor = "Crowde";
Q.commons_royalist += 3;
Q.burgher_royalist += 3;
Q.disfavored_royalist += 3;
Q.dufour_staal_r += 2;

Q.staal_approval += (Q.royalist_votes / 10);
Q.staal_approval -= (Q.marcher_votes / 10);
Q.staal_approval = Math.round(Q.staal_approval);

Q.staal_marcher_support -= 6;
Q.staal_marcher_r -= 4;
Q.staal_marcher_influence -= 3;
!}

Bram Frask is nominated to the Interior Ministry[? if old_heartland_leader == "Staal": —both in the Commonwealth and in Heartland?]. Garrick Crowde takes the vice-chancellorship—a title in name only. [? if heartland_leader == "Goodlake":  Although the <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**DSU**</span> would’ve preferred Crowde installed in Heartland, Goodlake stays on—as Staal’s loyal puppet and as a concession to the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>. ?]

At the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists’</span> insistence, Edrik Halbridge is brought in as an independent to head the Economic Ministry.

To compensate for the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>’s loss of influence, they're given an additional Ministry without Portfolio. Not that the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span> can complain—not with Hughes in charge.